:24:10.541','','2023-01-04 13:24:10.541',0,'','The original validity of registration in this case was 31.12.2021. After giving the benefit of six months on account of Covid-19 the validity stood extended upto 30.06.2022. The applicant in his explanatory note has requested that in addition to 6 months already granted, further extension in the validity may be granted upto 30.06.2023. Promoter has also submitted the indemnity bond regarding GST. It is pertinent to mention here that the promoter has provided copy of application dated 09.02.2022, for renewal of License to develop colony for this project along with details of fee paid for the same. Further promoter attached a copy of the request addressed to this Authority vide which the promoter stated that they are liable to submit LDC as and when received from the competent authority. As the promoter has provided license renewal application addressed to the Competent Authority i.e. GLADA, along with details of fees paid for renewal of said License, the matter is submitted for consideration/approval of extension for one year up to 30.06.2023, under section 6 of the Act.',2,0,'excgen3rera','2023-01-04 13:24:11.000','excgen3rera','2023-01-04 13:24:11.000'),(3581,150006,'excgen3rera','2023-01-04 13:29:54.000',1925,11101,'','FormE2022SAS0092','','','Authority Desk','Application CheckList Prepared','7b9d725a-b33c-4aba-934a-bee1ec13f684','','2023-01-04 13:29:53.213','','2023-01-04 13:29:53.213',0,'','The original validity of the registration, in this case, was 31.12.2022. The applicant in his explanatory note has requested further extension for one year i.e. up to   31.12.2023. The promoter has also submitted the indemnity bond regarding GST. The promoter has provided LDC which is valid up to 27.07.2025. Accordingly, the matter is submitted for consideration/approval of an extension in the validity of registration for one year up to 31.12.2023, under section 6 of the Act.',2,0,'excgen3rera','2023-01-04 13:29:54.000','excgen3r