demand letter dated 23.01.2023, issued by the Competent Authority i.e. PUDA, vide which PUDA asked the promoter to deposit the fee amounting to Rs. 11,17,600/- for an extension in the implementation period of the mega project and promoter has deposited the said fee vide DD No. 819036 dated 25.01.2023 (details of the same provided). Further, it is also stated that the promoter has provided letter dated 01.02.2023 in hard file which is issued by the PUDA, vide which the implementation period of the mega project is extended upto 31.12.2023. Accordingly, the matter is submitted for extension in the registration period, under section 6 of the Act up to 31.12.2023.',2,0,'excgen3rera','2023-02-07 09:43:46.000','excgen3rera','2023-02-07 09:43:46.000'),(3722,150006,'excgen3rera','2023-02-07 09:45:25.000',1056,10040,'','FormE2022SAS0099','','','Authority Desk','Application CheckList Prepared','7b9d725a-b33c-4aba-934a-bee1ec13f684','','2023-02-07 09:45:23.819','','2023-02-07 09:45:23.819',0,'','The original validity of the registration, in this case, was 31.12.2021. Which was further extended for six months up to 30.06.2022 on account of Covid-19, and was further extended up to 31.12.2022 (As per order of Hon,ble NCLT order dated 01.06.2021). The applicant in his explanatory note has requested that in addition to 6 months already granted, further extension in the validity may be granted up to 31.12.2024. But as per section 6 of the Act, only one-year extension is allowed which comes out to be up 31.12.2023. It is pertinent to mention here that the notification dated 06.01.2023 issued by the Department of Housing and Urban Development, Punjab has extended the implementation period of Mega Projects falls in the state of Punjab, up to 31.12.2023 subject to submission of the requisite fee. In this respect, the promoter has provided a copy of the demand letter dated 23.01.2023, issued by the Competent Authority i.e. PUDA, vide which PUDA asked the promoter to deposit the fee amount