rther extension under Section 6 till 04.10.2025. In this case, the applicant has provided the copy of NOC issued by EO, MC, Zirakpur dated 23.09.2024 which reveals that they have no objection if extension is granted by the RERA authority. However, a clarification was sought from the promoter / applicant asking them to to provide the NOC from the Competent Authority i.e. ADC (UD), SAS Nagar. In response thereof, the applicant / promoter has clarified that as per Punjab Municipal Act, 1911, EO of the concerned ULB is the sanctioning authority for all categories of building plans. The promoter further stated that the ADC(UD)\'s are the competent authority for approval of CLU/LDC under Section 81 of the PRTPD Act, 1995. The promoter further added that in this project, initial approval of the project was granted by MC, Zirakpur in the year 2008 and at that time, LCU certificate was not issued for the projects falls under the jurisdiction of local government and practice for issuance of the same was started in the year 2013.  He further added that the practice of issuance of LDC for areas falls under the jurisdiction of Local Government started in the year 2019. In this project, there is no CLU and LDC and has only building plan approval issued in the year 2008. It is also pertinent to note that the promoter has submitted that Occupancy Certificate qua this project issued by EO, MC, Zirakpur dated 24.10.2024.Therefore, considering the Occupancy Certificate and other facts stated by the applicant / promoter, the application for extension under Section 6 may be granted either till the request of the promoter i.e. upto 04.10.2025 or till the date of receipt of occupancy certificate i.e. upto 24.10.2024.	Accordingly, the case is submitted for consideration please.',2,0,'excgen4','2024-11-05 11:55:10.000','excgen4','2024-11-05 11:55:10.000'),(5940,150007,'ManagerIT.rera','2024-11-05 11:55:45.000',1421,10515,'','FormE2023LDH0085','','','Authority Desk','In-Complete Application 