. This project was registered offline and there is no change in the facts and documents since registration. Considering the fact that the period for which the extension is applied has already lapsed, it shall be prudent to facilitate further progress, development and completion of the project and in order to protect to the rights and interest of the allottees, the Authority took a lenient view and has decided to grant extension under section 6 of the Real Estate (Regulation and Development) Act, 2016 upto 30.04.2020. The Authority has directed that the promoter should be asked to apply for further extension under the relevant provisions of the RERD Act, 2016 or to submit completion certificate of the project. ',2,0,'excgen4','2025-07-16 10:52:51.000','excgen4','2025-07-16 10:52:51.000'),(6864,150006,'excgen4','2025-07-16 10:59:38.000',1330,10378,'','FormE2021SAS0043','','','Authority Desk','Application CheckList Prepared','7b9d725a-b33c-4aba-934a-bee1ec13f684','','2025-07-16 10:59:38.927','','2025-07-16 10:59:38.927',0,'','The application for extension u/s 6 of the RERD Act of this project was considered and approved by the Authority in the meeting held on 11.07.2025. The initial RERA registration of this project was valid till 30.04.2021, which was further extended due to COVID-19 in view of the Circular of this Authority till 30.10.2021. Consequent upon lapse of registration, the applicant / promoter has filed the said extension application online on 18.11.2021 with the request to grant extension in the validity of registration upto 30.10.2022. The promoter has provided the copy of License to Develop Colony dated 09.05.2018, which was valid till 08.05.2023.  During the meeting, the Authority was apprised to the fact that the Competent Authority has reduced the some portion of area from the project land and this office vide Memo No. RERA/Pb/EG(T)/2022/874 dated 10.02.2022, No. 1303 dated 28.02.2022, No. 2582 dated 28.03.2022 and No. 3623 dated 22.04.2022 has sought certain details / information from the promoter with regard to the reduction in the area. However, no response has been forthcoming from the promoter till date. The Authority after due deliberations and considering the best interest of the allottees and development of real estate sector has decided to grant extension under section 6 of the Real Estate (Regulation and Development) Act, 2016 upto30.10.2022 with the stipulation that the promoter cannot sell the inventory in the area which had been reduced by the Competent Authority. The Authority has further directed that the promoter should be asked to apply for further extension under the relevant provisions of the RERD Act, 2016 or to submit completion certificate of the project. \r\n',2,0,'excgen4','2025-07-16 10:59:38.000','excgen4','2025-07-16 10:59:38.000'),(6865,150006,'excgen4','2025-07-16 11:09:30.000',1916,11093,'','FormE2023SAS0138','','','Authority Desk','Application CheckList Prepared','7b9d725a-b33c-4aba-934a-bee1ec13f684','','2025-07-16 11:09:31.292','','2025-07-16 11:09:31.292',0,'','The application for extension under section 6 of the RERD Act of this project was taken up for consideration and approved by the Authority in the meeting 11.07.2025. The RERA registration of this project was valid till 30.06.2023. Consequent upon lapse of registration, the applicant / promoter has filed the said extension application online on 31.12.2023 with the request to grant extension in the validity of registration upto 30.06.2024. The promoter has provided the copy of License to Develop Colony dated 16.06.2020, which was valid till 15.06.2025. The Authority after due deliberations and considering the best interest of the allottees and development of real estate sector has decided to grant extension under section 6 of the RERD Act, 2016 upto 30.06.2024. The Authority has further directed that the promoter should be asked to apply for further extension under the relevant provisions of the RERD Act, 2016 or to submit completion certificate of the project. \r\n',2,0,'excgen4','2025-07-16 11:09:30.000','excgen4','2025-07-16 11:09:30.000'),(6866,150006,'excgen4','2025-07-16 11:24:16.000',1963,11139,'','FormE2024BTI0037','','','Authority Desk','Application CheckList Prepared','7b9d725a-b33c-4aba-934a-bee1ec13f684','','2025-07-16 11:24:16.981','','2025-07-16 11:24:16.981',0,'','The application for extension under sec 6 of the RERD Act of this project was considered and approved by the Authority in the meeting dated 11.07.2025. The RERA registration of this project was valid till 30.12.2019. Consequent upon lapse of registration, the applicant / promoter has filed the said extension application online on 24.05.2024 with the request to grant extension in the validity of registration upto 30.12.2020. The promoter has provided renewed copy of License to Develop Colony which was valid till 26.12.2022. It was noted by the Authority that a penalty has also been imposed under Chapter VIII of the RERD Act in relation to the said project. However, separate proceedings / action for the recovery of this amount is being taken in accordance with the provisions of RERD Act and Rules thereunder and as per the Punjab Land Revenue Act, 1887. Therefore, it would not be appropriate to withhold the application of the promoter for extension u/s 6 on this ground. Thus, the Authority after due deliberations and considering the best interest of the allottees and development of real estate sector has decided to grant extension under section 6 of the Real Estate RERD Act, 2016 upto 30.12.2020. The Authority has further directed that the promoter should be asked to apply for further extension under the relevant provisions of the RERD Act, 2016 or to submit completion certificate of the project. ',2,0,'excgen4','2025-07-16 11:24:16.000','excgen4','2025-07-16 11:24:16.000'),(6867,150006,'excgen4','2025-07-16 11:27:43.000',1760,10942,'','FormE2023LDH0083','','','Authority Desk','Application CheckList Prepared','7b