eckList Prepared','7b9d725a-b33c-4aba-934a-bee1ec13f684','','2026-05-11 10:04:38.165','','2026-05-11 10:04:38.165',0,'','Check list prepared with observations.',2,0,'excgen4','2026-05-11 10:04:34.000','excgen4','2026-05-11 10:04:34.000'),(8526,150006,'excgen4','2026-05-11 10:05:35.000',1321,10898,'','FormE2026SAS0012','','','Authority Desk','Application CheckList Prepared','7b9d725a-b33c-4aba-934a-bee1ec13f684','','2026-05-11 10:05:38.596','','2026-05-11 10:05:38.596',0,'','Check list prepared with observation.',2,0,'excgen4','2026-05-11 10:05:35.000','excgen4','2026-05-11 10:05:35.000'),(8527,150006,'excgen4','2026-05-11 13:03:51.000',2534,11193,'','FormE2026SAS0013','','','Authority Desk','Application CheckList Prepared','7b9d725a-b33c-4aba-934a-bee1ec13f684','','2026-05-11 13:03:54.705','','2026-05-11 13:03:54.705',0,'','The original validity of the registration of this project is up to 31.12.2025. The applicant in his explanatory note has requested extension for one year i.e. up to 31.12.2026 and also copies of NOCs are provided. Promoter/applicant has submitted renewed license to develop colony dated 29.04.2026 which is valid upto 31.12.2028 issued to the promoter M/s Curo India Pvt. Ltd. along with letter dated 25.03.2026. issued by GMADA regarding Permission to M/s SRG Marbella Developer and Promoters LLP to join as a co promoter into the project. It is pertinent to mention here that as per Revised registration letter dated 19.12.2022 Authority has considered M/s SRG Marbella Developers and Promoters LLP as promoter not co promoter but as per GMADA letter dated 25.03.2026 the same is considered as co promoter only. Clarification regarding same is submitted by the promoter. Accordingly, the matter is submitted for consideration/approval of extension in registration period of this project for one year i.e. up to 31.12.2026, under section 6 of the Act.',2,0,'excgen4','2026-05-11 13:03:51.000','excgen4','2026-05-11 13:03:51.000'),(8528,150007,'DirectorIT','2026-05-11 14:51:33.000',2692,11805,'','FormE2026LDH0014','','','Authority Desk','In-Complete Application (Additional Information Sought by the Authority)','15ac7786-a35e-46a3-ae19-8befd003dcfd','','2026-05-11 14:51:37.145','','2026-05-11 14:51:37.145',0,'','The application you filed for the extension of project registration is found to be incomplete. After examining the application, observations have been shared with you on your dashboard on the authority\'s web portal. Therefore, your application is being returned with a notice explaining why it may not be rejected due to the deficiencies pointed out in the observations. You are hereby allowed to be heard as per proviso 2 to section 6 of the RERD Act, 2016. Further,  you are also allowed to remove the deficiencies and inaccuracies and submit proper documents online within 5 days of the return of the application. Further, you are hereby allowed to be heard in person or through your representative by the Real Estate Regulatory Authority, Punjab, in the Conference Room, First Floor, Block-B, Plot No. 3, Madhya Marg, Sector 18-A, Chandigarh, on 26.05.2026 at 2.30 pm. In the event of failure to submit a proper reply, non-appearance for hearing, or submission of an incomplete response, the Authority may be constrained to take appropriate action, including rejection of the application for extension of registration of the project, without granting any further opportunity',1,0,'DirectorIT','2026-05-11 14:51:33.000','DirectorIT','2026-05-11 14:51:33.000'),(8529,150007,'DirectorIT','2026-05-11 14:52:05.000',1321,10898,'','FormE2026SAS0012','','','Authority Desk','In-Complete Application (Additional Information Sought by the Authority)','15ac7786-a35e-46a3-ae19-8befd003dcfd','','2026-05-11 14:52:08.713','','2026-05-11 14:52:08.713',0,'','The application you filed for the extension of project registration is found to be incomplete. After examining the application, observations have been shared with you on your dashboard on the authority\'s web portal. Therefore, your application is being returned with a notice explaining why it may not be rejected due to the deficiencies pointed out in the observations. You are hereby allowed to be heard as per proviso 2 to section 6 of the RERD Act, 2016. Further,  you are also allowed to remove the deficiencies and inaccuracies and submit proper documents online within 5 days of the return of the application. Further, you are hereby allowed to be heard in person or through your representative by the Real Estate Regulatory Authority, Punjab, in the Conference Room, First Floor, Block-B, Plot No. 3, Madhya Marg, Sector 18-A, Chandigarh, on 26.05.2026 at 2.30 pm. In the event of failure to submit a proper reply, non-appearance for hearing, or submission of an incomplete response, the Authority may be constrained to take appropriate action, including rejection of the application for extension of registration of the project, without granting any further opportunity',1,0,'DirectorIT','2026-05-11 14:52:05.000','DirectorIT','2026-05-11 14:52:05.000'),(8530,150034,'DirectorIT','2026-05-11 15:22:50.000',2534,11193,'','FormE2026SAS0013','','','Authority Desk','Application CheckList Verified and Forward to Secretary RERA','15ac7786-a35e-46a3-ae19-8befd003dcfd','','2026-05-11 15:22:53.592','','2026-05-11 15:22:53.592',0,'','Please refer to the office note above. The registration is valid upto 31.12.2025.  The extension is applied upto 31.12.2026. The promoter has submitted License to Develop valid upto 31.12.2028. The promoter has submitted NOC of AAI, PSPCL, PPCB and EC with his revision application. Forest Road access is provided with the extension application. Further the promoter in is explanatory note stated the project was delayed due to revision of the layout plans was necessary for making the project viable and it took considerable time getting the revised layout plan approved.  As per the architect certificate negligible progress has been made with regard to the common areas and facilities whereas with respect to excavation, basement, stilt work has been completed more than 50 percent.  As regard the inclusion of the promoter as co promoter by GMADA and the explanation submitted by the promoter may be considered. As such the both PAPRA and RERA act do not distinguish co-promoter from the promoter and shall be jointly liable for all functions and responsibilities specified under the Act, rules and regulations for the purposes of RERA.  Submitted for further orders and consideration, please',1,0,'DirectorIT','2026-05-11 15:22:50.000','DirectorIT','2026-05-11 15:22:50.000');
